and as time was up and she turned in her  contracts final exam she realized she  was in the wrong class and she had done  the wrong final today we're talking  about real life law school horror  stories ooh scary  [Music]  hey legal eagles D James Stone here  teaching you how to think like a lawyer  so you can crush law school law school  can be a really scary place it's three  years long and in that time a lot can go  wrong so I thought I'd share some of the  scariest things that actually happened  to me in law school so let's dig into  some of these scary stories one of the  first things that happens when you get  to law school is that you are surrounded  by some of the smartest people you've  ever met in your entire life I don't  really care which law school it is  you're gonna be surrounded by a type  personalities and some of those people  are what are called Gunners Gunners are  the people that always raise their hand  they always seem to have the answer and  when you first get to law school they  can seem really intimidating because  people don't like to answer the  professor's questions so I had a few  Gunners in my class hopefully I was not  one of those Gunners even though I'd  liked to answer on occasion but there  was one particular gunner in my class  for the sake of an amenity let's call  him Alan Alan was hardcore he would  answer every professor's question he had  a background in mathematics and  philosophy so he was able to talk about  the philosophical underpinnings of  different legal doctrines he was able to  think logically and he always seemed to  have the answer so after your first  semester you are given a slip of paper  with your grades in it and I happen to  be sitting behind Alan in class in  between classes when we were getting our  grades for the first time basically you  open up a slip a  and that's your report card and I happen  to see that he got all C's his first  semester I was shocked I I had never  seen anything like it one of if not the  smartest person in class got all C's let  it be a lesson to you that just because  someone is very good in class and seems  to be one of the smartest people in the  room it doesn't mean they're gonna get  good grades in law school and this  person eventually became a friend of  mine but man it was it was quite a shock  to see that this person who seemed to  know all the answers got straight C's  his first semester another horror story  that happened to me relates to my mock  trial competition I was on the mock  trial team for all three years in law  school I was one of the best experiences  that I had  mock trial is where you pretend to be a  lawyer you conduct a trial and you are  scored by judges based on how well you  do it's just like mock trial in high  school and college and part of the mock  trial competition is traveling to  different cities well one of the  competitions was held in Las Vegas in  fact it was one of the national finals  for this particular mock trial  competition and after my team had done  their round and we had actually  conducted around in front of a real  judge who actually tried cases in Las  Vegas the mock trial judge started to  brag to my team and the other team about  what happened one night when a burglar  tried to break into his house so this  sitting judge regaled us for about 15  minutes about how an intruder tried to  break into his house and what he did  with this intruder well apparently to  hear this judge tell the tale he sat the  intruder down on a chair tied him up put  him in a small bathroom and then for the  next hour or two proceeded to threaten  him with a gun to his head  and told him never to come back to his  house I'm guessing that if that actually  happened that that burglar never burgled  that guy's house again and this is again  a sitting judge I don't know if that's a  true story or not this was Vegas after  all so I probably believe that this  judge is an insane person who threatened  a burglar with a firearm so that was  that was an interesting experience  another horror story that happened to me  was that when I was sitting for the  California Bar Exam it was at a hotel in  in West LA and not just in the regular  part of the hotel but three floors down  in the basement and this was a huge  cavern I mean there must have been five  hundred people at least sitting for this  exam and so on day one of the exam we  were into the second essay portion of  the bar exam and all of a sudden as what  happens in California everything started  to shake there was an earthquake I later  learned that it was over a 5.0 on the  Richter scale so it was enough to get  the chandeliers in in the basement to  swing back and forth and all of the  people who were not native Californians  hid under their desk and you know were  shaken literally and figuratively and  and they lost some crucial time on the  bar exam I am the rest of the native  Californians just simply couldn't be  bothered and carried along writing our  essays so I actually feel that that gave  me an advantage on the bar exam because  I think the people who from out of town  were for a little bit frazzled whereas  being a native Southern Californian it  was just a normal Tuesday afternoon for  me so so I give partial credit to the  earthquake for helping me pass the  California Bar Exam another horror story  that happened to me was that my computer  crashed  right before finals so this was over 11  or 12 years ago so this is back in the  day when computers didn't have  solid-state hard drives and Dropbox and  Google Drive did not exist so I was  relying on the files that were  physically residing on my computer and  my hard drive just stopped working there  were clear signs that something was  going wrong so I had the the wherewithal  to transfer some of these these files to  I don't know a floppy disk or a zip  drive or maybe I burned it to a CD I'm  not sure but I was able to get my notes  off of the computer probably about 45  minutes before the thing just stopped  and never started up again so I got  really lucky it still was very frazzling  I lost a lot of files just before finals  in my second year of law school but  that's why I am very adamant to current  and future law students to always use  cloud services backup your files there's  a chance that you will never get them  back I mean laptops fail they're stolen  all the time you never know when your  computer is going to crash and you can  bet that it's probably going to happen  at the worst possible time so do  yourself a favor and backup your crucial  files and my final law school horror  story is that after three years of law  school over six semesters I graduated  with over a hundred and sixty thousand  dollars in debt yeah that's more than a  lot of people's houses cost that's three  BMWs worth of debt and that was over ten  years ago now law school tuition has  gone up even more so I really feel for  all the the current law students that  are out there who are racking up law  school debt it's it's crazy it's it's  everyone's personal Horror Story it took  me years to pay it off and it really  impacted my quality of life I don't  regret going to law school but all the  debt that you accumulate really does  build up  and man it's it's tough so those were  just a few of the horror stories that I  exper Sinhalese in law school if you  want to hear more stories about law  school check out this short playlist  that I put together that includes my  personal experiences with law school and  even better strategies on how to beat  law school once you get in and how to  get A's in law school also please  subscribe really appreciate it and I'll  see you in the next video
 

